        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "50ed3442-1287-5c95-a1f6-7f9101531194",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Starrcade (1992), BattleBowl/The Lethal Lottery II\n- Places: The Omni, Atlanta, Georgia\n- People: Ron Simmons, \"Dr. Death\" Steve Williams, Shane Douglas, Ricky Steamboat, Brian Pillman, Barry Windham, Masahiro Chono, The Great Muta\n- Organizations: WCW, NWA\n- Championships: WCW World Heavyweight Championship, WCW World Tag Team Championship, NWA World Heavyweight Championship\n- Roles: professional wrestler, author, collegiate football player, amateur wrestler\n\nFacts:\n- Steven Williams was born on May 14, 1960, and he later became better known by the ring name \"Dr. Death\" Steve Williams.\n- Steve Williams was an American professional wrestler, author, former collegiate football player, and amateur wrestler at the University of Oklahoma.\n- Starrcade (1992), also called BattleBowl/The Lethal Lottery II, took place on December 28, 1992, as a major annual professional wrestling pay-per-view show.\n- Starrcade (1992) was held at The Omni in Atlanta, Georgia.\n- At Starrcade (1992), Ron Simmons defended the WCW World Heavyweight Championship against Steve Williams.\n- At Starrcade (1992), Shane Douglas and Ricky Steamboat defended the WCW World Tag Team Championship against Brian Pillman and Barry Windham.\n- At Starrcade (1992), Masahiro Chono defended the NWA World Heavyweight Championship against The Great Muta.\n- Steve Williams died on December 29, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "35eb51a8-cb38-559a-bd7b-a05147f07edb",
        "text": "Page: Starrcade (1992). Sentence: Starrcade (1992): BattleBowl/The Lethal Lottery II was a major annual professional wrestling show, broadcast on pay-per-view (PPV) that took place on December 28, 1992, from The Omni in Atlanta, Georgia.\nPage: Starrcade (1992). Sentence: The show also saw Ron Simmons defend the WCW World Heavyweight Championship against \"Dr. Death\" Steve Williams, the team of Shane Douglas and Ricky Steamboat putting the WCW World Tag Team Championship on the line against the team of Brian Pillman and Barry Windham and Masahiro Chono defend the NWA World Heavyweight Championship against The Great Muta.\nPage: &quot;Dr. Death&quot; Steve Williams. Sentence: Steven Williams (May 14, 1960 – December 29, 2009), better known by his ring name \"Dr. Death\" Steve Williams, was an American professional wrestler, author, former collegiate football player, and amateur wrestler at the University of Oklahoma.",
